{
 "_about": "The Switch Axe's phial effects as the ROM requests them: the effect holder's rows, the burst shells' rows, the\nrequester's codes and the colour tables -- written to the Armor Viewer as docs/effects/w08-shells.json.\nRead 2026-09-28, corrected 2026-09-29 (the bursts' sites, the fixed palette, the decimal motion ids).\n\n    python tools/w08shells.py                 writes docs/effects/w08-shells.json\n    python tools/w08shells.py <out.json>      writes elsewhere (to compare before replacing the shipped file)\n\nThe rows come straight from romfs shell/pl/w08.arc (player/plshells.py reads any class the same way); the colour\ntables from loc/arc/resident.arc and the stage arcs.\n\nWHAT IS IN IT (every number read out of the ROM or its data, the addresses are main.text):\n  holder      shell/pleffect/effect_w08 rows: the effect-holder shell uShellPlEffectW08 (vtable 0x1756e00). The player\n              keeps one at +0x2634; a request names a ROW (\"code\") of this list and takes its spec 0: vtable +0x39c =\n              0x281ef4 -> holder +0x150 = 0x44bfcc (fire and forget); vtable +0x3a0 = 0x281f14 -> holder +0x154 =\n              0x44c0c4 (a tracked slot, replacing what it held); 0x281ffc -> holder +0x158 = 0x44c164 (a tracked slot,\n              idempotent). The holder's stop policy is its vtable +0x160 = 0x454ed4, per code.\n  requester   uPlayerQuest08's 0x11a40f4(self, mode): mode -> code. The phial (player parameter 27, the equipment's copy\n              of weapon08BaseData mBinType, read through vtable +0x15c) picks the EVEN code for Dragon ([2,4,6,10][mode])\n              and the ODD one for every other phial ([1,3,5,9][mode]) plus a colour: entry [8,9,10,0,12,11][phial]\n              (rodata 0x16a76b0) of the FIXED table `palettes.player` into the request block +0x80 with override bit\n              17; mode 4 would be code 13 with no colour (no call site passes 4: row 13 is asked by 0x11a30c4 itself). The parent is the unit in the player's part slot 7 (+0x23a0: the\n              first weapon unit) and the root joint is overridden to 0 (block +0x52, bit 5). WHICH MOTIONS ASK is in the\n              Armor Viewer's render/weapon-fx.js SWORD_REQUESTS (motion ids are decimal bank*1000+slot; an earlier\n              `motionsSeen` block here listed hex-split numbers and is gone).\n  burst000/1  shell/pl/pl_w08_000 (uShellPlw08_000, shell id 0x2e) and pl_w08_001 (0x2f) rows: each row's record(s).\n              The shells are CREATED by two sites of the class (0x48b884 with the shell id and the row in the setup\n              block): 0x119eecc on Motion[125] at frame 12 and 0x11a38d0 on Motion[137] at frame 2, the row chosen\n              by phial and element; the shell's init (vtable +0x13c = 0x474330 / 0x474c54) requests spec 0 of its row.\n              The class's many 0x2b6a80 sites register attack HITBOXES, not shells: an earlier reading here took them\n              for the shells' spawns.\n  palettes    rProofEffectColorControl tables. `player` = loc/arc/resident.arc effect/pec/pec_001, the effect manager's\n              colour-control slot 1, which every phial colour is read from; `resident` = all five resident tables;\n              `stages` = each stage arc's own table (slot 0: other effects' tints), kept for reference.\n              THE APP READS `palettes.player`: a file without it draws no coloured aura at all (the ROM makes no\n              request when the table has no entry, and so does render/weapon-fx.js colourFor).",
